@startuml wasm-shield
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam rectangleBorderThickness 2
skinparam ArrowThickness 2
skinparam nodesep 20
skinparam ranksep 30

title Host Process vs WASM: Attack Surface Comparison

' --- Attacks on left ---
together {
    rectangle "Read env vars\n(steal API keys)" as ATK1 #ff7675
    rectangle "Fetch to attacker.com\n(exfiltrate data)" as ATK2 #ff7675
    rectangle "Read ~/.ssh/id_rsa\n(steal credentials)" as ATK3 #ff7675
    rectangle "Spawn reverse shell\n(persistent access)" as ATK4 #ff7675
}

' --- Host process in middle ---
rectangle "**Host Process**\n(TypeScript tool)" as HOST #FFEAA7

' --- WASM on right ---
rectangle "**WASM Module**\n(Extism plugin)" as WASM #DFE6E9

ATK1 -right-> HOST : <color:red>**✓ succeeds**</color>\nprocess.env.*
ATK2 -right-> HOST : <color:red>**✓ succeeds**</color>\nfetch() unrestricted
ATK3 -right-> HOST : <color:red>**✓ succeeds**</color>\nfs.readFile()
ATK4 -right-> HOST : <color:red>**✓ succeeds**</color>\nchild_process.exec()

ATK1 -right-> WASM : <color:green>**✗ no env API**</color>
ATK2 -right-> WASM : <color:green>**✗ allowedHosts: []**</color>
ATK3 -right-> WASM : <color:green>**✗ allowedPaths: []**</color>
ATK4 -right-> WASM : <color:green>**✗ no shell exists**</color>

note bottom of HOST
  4/4 attacks succeed.
  Tool must be **trusted**.
end note

note bottom of WASM
  0/4 attacks succeed.
  Capabilities **don't exist**
  unless explicitly granted.
end note

@enduml
